# Plugin: Systematic Debugging Adapter

Purpose:
  Adapt Superpowers systematic debugging skill for SDDRA bugfix/hotfix chains.

Source:
  D:\Tasks\ai_code\vkard.az\tmp\external-repo-audit\repo-01\skills\systematic-debugging\SKILL.md

Original:
  Four phases:
    1. Root Cause Investigation
    2. Hypothesis Formation
    3. Fix Implementation
    4. Verification

  Iron Law: NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST

Adapted for SDDRA:
  Mapped to bugfix/hotfix chain stages:
    Phase 1 (Root Cause) -> AR (Architecture) stage
    Phase 2 (Hypothesis) -> AR stage continuation
    Phase 3 (Fix) -> BE (Backend) stage
    Phase 4 (Verify) -> VR (Verify) stage

  Iron Law adapted:
    NO CODE CHANGE WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST

  Integration:
    - AR stage in bugfix chain enhanced with 4-phase investigation
    - Decision record created for root cause
    - Verification criteria from investigation

  Evidence gathering:
    - Error logs from .sdd/instances/vkard.az/observability/
    - Recent changes from .sdd/decisions/
    - Dependency graph from .sdd/instances/vkard.az/dependencies/

Usage:
  Referenced by:
    .sdd/chains/bugfix.sdd (AR stage)
    .sdd/chains/hotfix.sdd (AR stage)
    .sdd/chains/incident.sdd (AR stage)

  Triggers:
    - Bug report
    - Test failure
    - Production incident

State: Adapted
